{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>אכף</b> — [means] caused and brought about. That is, the soul of one who labors will labor continually all his days, for his mouth's אכף brought about and caused upon him labor, because he did not learn words of pleasantness. The opposite of this: wisdom gives life to its possessor."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:12.346728384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}